# the command tools — so `new_agent` is `sensitive` (a card in `ask` mode, in THIS agent's pane),
# `send_to_agent` and `stop_agent` are `standard`, `read_agent` is `safe`. Which agent is asking is
# never an argument: it rides beside them as this bridge's token, and the shell holds the caller to
# it — a child cannot start agents of its own, an agent holds at most three, and an agent directs
# and reads only the agents it started. `pass` names the arguments that go through as they are.
